{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken","id":1524668,"title":"Is Blood Sorcery Totally Broken?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-28T18:55:00-07:00","id":1524668,"title":"Is Blood Sorcery Totally Broken?","content":"Hello, I've recently been reading through the Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies book for vtr. Note, I am looking at this from a 2e perspective, since it is mentioned within the corebook and supplement books. Although it takes 30 minutes per roll on rituals, I am seeing a number of problems with how the system is working, please let me know if I'm missing something, or if this is entirely broken. <br /> <br /> A starting vampire with Manipulation and Occult 5 can roll 10 + Cruac Theme dice for their rituals, and can roll up to 10 + Cruac Theme times (unmodified dice pool). Does this not mean that they could target some insane amount of Potency and roll 30+ successes as an extended action to buff themselves with Transmutation or Protection, or deal a vastly unreasonable amount of damage? Yes it takes time so you can't use it in a fight, but why fight when you can use Destruction from miles away, or prepare your Protection rituals beforehand so no one can hit you? <br /> <br /> Please let me know if I'm misinterpreting these rules somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T19:33:30-07:00","id":1524670,"title":"","content":"Sacraments and Blasphemies is a first edition book. The rules were updated to 2nd edition by Chris Falco in Rites of Damnation. I believe None More Dark has also used that for some of their spell casting options, although their latest book eschews that option and goes back to stand core blood magic for Kindred Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I can't tell you if your understanding of the rules is correct or not though, I haven't read either of those books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 10-28-2023, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T20:14:44-07:00","id":1524674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken#post1524668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A starting vampire with Manipulation and Occult 5</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though you have already jumped too far when your assumption for something being &quot;broken&quot; involves a starting character with Traits at the cap. You're talking about one of the most charming people in the world with one of the strongest grasps of the supernatural that doesn't require superhuman potential.<br /> <br /> Free Theme dots are similarly focused; if you don't buy extra dots in Destruction, the only way you're getting Destruction 3 at Cr\u00faac 3 is if both of your other Themes are at 1, which combines with the above to get a firm &quot;no duh&quot; response to a statement that is, effectively, &quot;if you bend your character's entire build toward specializing in doing this well, you can do some incredible things.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does this not mean that they could target some insane amount of Potency and roll 30+ successes as an extended action to buff themselves with Transmutation or Protection, or deal a vastly unreasonable amount of damage? </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that particularly useful effects are generally gated behind at least the third dot of a Theme, and 2e's adjustments to the roll interval also introduces the edition's Condition-based complication for failed rolls that in this case specifically applies a notable penalty to all subsequent rolls, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T23:38:13-07:00","id":1524675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken?p=1524674#post1524674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though you have already jumped too far when your assumption for something being &quot;broken&quot; involves a starting character with Traits at the cap. You're talking about one of the most charming people in the world with one of the strongest grasps of the supernatural that doesn't require superhuman potential.<br /> <br /> Free Theme dots are similarly focused; if you don't buy extra dots in Destruction, the only way you're getting Destruction 3 at Cr\u00faac 3 is if both of your other Themes are at 1, which combines with the above to get a firm &quot;no duh&quot; response to a statement that is, effectively, &quot;if you bend your character's entire build toward specializing in doing this well, you can do some incredible things.&quot;<br /> <br /> With the caveat that particularly useful effects are generally gated behind at least the third dot of a Theme, and 2e's adjustments to the roll interval also introduces the edition's Condition-based complication for failed rolls that in this case specifically applies a notable penalty to all subsequent rolls, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that being at the peak of human capability means that you should be able to do incredible things. However, the way the system is written, you can make a number of rolls equal to you unmodified dicepool, meaning an absurd number of successes can be garnered. According to the system, a vampire even with Manipulation 3, Occult 3, Theme 3, is rolling 9 dice, 9 times, for a total of 81 dice. Meaning that they would get 27 successes on average. With Protection or Transmutation, they can buff themselves to an absurd degree. I understand that this was based on the Mage 1e system, however it's explicitly referenced and used in Secrets of the Covenants and the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T00:20:30-07:00","id":1524677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken?p=1524670#post1524670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sacraments and Blasphemies is a first edition book. The rules were updated to 2nd edition by Chris Falco in Rites of Damnation. I believe None More Dark has also used that for some of their spell casting options, although their latest book eschews that option and goes back to stand core blood magic for Kindred Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I can't tell you if your understanding of the rules is correct or not though, I haven't read either of those books.</div> </div> </div> </div>We use the vanilla system in <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected Revised </b>for ease of use, but we're going to be using the reworked blood sorcery system in <b>Requiem for Rome 2E </b>going forward, which (for those who haven't read it) reduces Ritual Disciplines to a single roll but keeps the extended casting time of 2E. Potency is determined by a dice penalty rather than a random die result. The <b>RFR2E </b>system is fully backwards compatible with previous 2E rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T01:54:10-08:00","id":1526549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken?p=1524677#post1524677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We use the vanilla system in <b>Bloodlines: The Resurrected Revised </b>for ease of use, but we're going to be using the reworked blood sorcery system in <b>Requiem for Rome 2E </b>going forward, which (for those who haven't read it) reduces Ritual Disciplines to a single roll but keeps the extended casting time of 2E. Potency is determined by a dice penalty rather than a random die result. The <b>RFR2E </b>system is fully backwards compatible with previous 2E rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you guys have plans on publishing the new system? I really enjoyed Rome Blood Sorcery, would love to see how it works under the hood. And maybe even let players use it as something like creative thamathurgy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","user":"ImortalKiller","date":".  Fixing quote 12-14-2023, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T14:21:05-08:00","id":1526813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ImortalKiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken?p=1526549#post1526549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you guys have plans on publishing the new system? I really enjoyed Rome Blood Sorcery, would love to see how it works under the hood. And maybe even let players use it as something like creative thamathurgy</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we'll probably get a bit more into it with the Crone book (and the Lancea), where we may want to finesse a couple of the older rites to work better with the new system. It IS backwards compatible, but there might be some quality-of-life updates we could make. We don't have any specific plans for a blood sorcery book, but you never know!<br /> <br /> (sorry for the very late reply, I didn't get a notification!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T14:59:23-08:00","id":1526815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken?p=1526813#post1526813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we'll probably get a bit more into it with the Crone book (and the Lancea), where we may want to finesse a couple of the older rites to work better with the new system. It IS backwards compatible, but there might be some quality-of-life updates we could make. We don't have any specific plans for a blood sorcery book, but you never know!<br /> <br /> (sorry for the very late reply, I didn't get a notification!)</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, and probably, I did something wrong, I don't know how to use the forum very well \ud83d\ude25<br /> <br /> But that aside, you really got me hyped for the books, hope they come out soon.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T13:59:36-08:00","id":1526874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524668-is-blood-sorcery-totally-broken?p=1526813#post1526813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we'll probably get a bit more into it with the Crone book (and the Lancea), where we may want to finesse a couple of the older rites to work better with the new system. It IS backwards compatible, but there might be some quality-of-life updates we could make. We don't have any specific plans for a blood sorcery book, but you never know!<br /> <br /> (sorry for the very late reply, I didn't get a notification!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yo none more dark publishing teaser","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}